["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasDependencyManifest", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The `from` Element has manifest files that contain dependency information in each `to` Element.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iswc", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Musical Work Code (ISWC)](https://www.iswc.org/iswc) is an 11-character unique identifier standardized by [ISO 15707](https://www.iso.org/standard/83125.html) for musical works (compositions) as distinct from specific recordings. While the \"ISWC\" label and grouping separators (dots and hyphens) are used for human readability, they shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `T0017812031`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/ConfidentialityLevelType/amberStrict", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Limited distribution - organization only. The dataset shall be shared only with specific organizations on a need-to-know basis.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/describes", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The `from` Element describes each `to` Element. To denote the root(s) of a tree of elements in a collection, the rootElement property shall be used.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N72785d5776d54ece8f6880490a7ea60c", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/securityAdvisory", "globalId", "", ""]
